.TH "MINIOS\-CMD" "1" "August 2026" "MiniOS Command\-Line Builder" ""
.SH NAME
minios\-cmd \- command\-line utility for configuring and building
customized MiniOS system images
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]minios\-cmd\f[R] [\f[I]OPTIONS\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]minios\-cmd\f[R] is a command\-line utility designed to simplify
the process of configuring and building customized MiniOS system images.
Acting as a frontend for \f[B]minios\-live\f[R](1), it manages the
configuration and invokes \f[B]minios\-live\f[R] to execute the actual
build steps.
.SS Build Options
With \f[B]minios\-cmd\f[R], you can customize various aspects of your
MiniOS image, including:
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Distribution:\f[R] Choose from Debian releases (\f[B]buster\f[R],
\f[B]bullseye\f[R], \f[B]bookworm\f[R], \f[B]trixie\f[R]) and Ubuntu
releases (\f[B]jammy\f[R], \f[B]noble\f[R])
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Architecture:\f[R] Specify the target architecture
(\f[B]amd64\f[R], \f[B]i386\f[R] for older distributions)
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Desktop Environment:\f[R]
.RS 2
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Debian:\f[R] \f[B]xfce\f[R] (standard), \f[B]flux\f[R] (minimum),
\f[B]lxqt\f[R] (bookworm/trixie only)
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Ubuntu:\f[R] \f[B]xfce\f[R] only
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Package Variant:\f[R]
.RS 2
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]All Debian:\f[R] \f[B]standard\f[R] (xfce), \f[B]minimum\f[R]
(flux)
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Bookworm/Trixie only:\f[R] \f[B]toolbox\f[R], \f[B]ultra\f[R]
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Ubuntu:\f[R] \f[B]standard\f[R] only
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Compression Type:\f[R] Specify the image compression method
(\f[B]zstd\f[R])
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Kernel:\f[R] Select a distribution or AUFS\-enabled MiniOS kernel
and compile optional DKMS modules
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Locale and Timezone:\f[R] Set the system locale and timezone with
multilingual support
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Configuration Options
.TP
\f[B]\-\-config\-file\f[R] \f[I]FILE\f[R]
Specify the configuration file path.
All other options are ignored.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-config\-only\f[R]
Generate the configuration file only and do not start the build process.
.SS Build Options
.TP
\f[B]\-b\f[R], \f[B]\-\-build\-dir\f[R] \f[I]DIR\f[R]
Specify the build directory.
.SS System Options
These options \f[B]must be provided\f[R] unless a configuration file is
used:
.TP
\f[B]\-d\f[R], \f[B]\-\-distribution\f[R] \f[I]NAME\f[R]
Specify the distribution name (e.g., `bookworm').
\f[B]REQUIRED\f[R]
.TP
\f[B]\-a\f[R], \f[B]\-\-architecture\f[R] \f[I]NAME\f[R]
Specify the architecture (e.g., `amd64').
\f[B]REQUIRED\f[R]
.TP
\f[B]\-de\f[R], \f[B]\-\-desktop\-environment\f[R] \f[I]NAME\f[R]
Specify the desktop environment (e.g., `xfce').
\f[B]REQUIRED\f[R]
.TP
\f[B]\-pv\f[R], \f[B]\-\-package\-variant\f[R] \f[I]NAME\f[R]
Specify the package variant (e.g., `standard').
\f[B]REQUIRED\f[R]
.TP
\f[B]\-c\f[R], \f[B]\-\-compression\-type\f[R] \f[I]NAME\f[R]
Specify the compression type (e.g., `zstd').
.SS Kernel Options
.TP
\f[B]\-kp\f[R], \f[B]\-\-kernel\-provider\f[R] \f[I]NAME\f[R]
Select the kernel provider (`distribution' or `minios').
.TP
\f[B]\-kf\f[R], \f[B]\-\-kernel\-flavour\f[R] \f[I]NAME\f[R]
Specify the kernel flavour (e.g., `none').
.TP
\f[B]\-mk\f[R], \f[B]\-\-minios\-kernel\f[R]
Install the AUFS\-enabled MiniOS kernel.
.TP
\f[B]\-mks\f[R], \f[B]\-\-minios\-kernel\-series\f[R] \f[I]NAME\f[R]
Select the MiniOS kernel series (`auto', `6.1', or `6.12') and use the
MiniOS provider.
.TP
\f[B]\-kpm\f[R], \f[B]\-\-kernel\-payload\-mode\f[R] \f[I]NAME\f[R]
Select the kernel payload mode (`runtime' or `full').
.TP
\f[B]\-dkms\f[R], \f[B]\-\-kernel\-build\-dkms\f[R]
Enable compilation of additional drivers during kernel installation.
.SS Locale and Timezone Options
.TP
\f[B]\-l\f[R], \f[B]\-\-locale\f[R] \f[I]NAME\f[R]
Specify the system locale (e.g., `en_US').
.TP
\f[B]\-ml\f[R], \f[B]\-\-multilingual\f[R]
Enable multilingual support.
.TP
\f[B]\-kl\f[R], \f[B]\-\-keep\-locales\f[R]
Keep all available locales.
.TP
\f[B]\-tz\f[R], \f[B]\-\-timezone\f[R] \f[I]NAME\f[R]
Specify the timezone (e.g., `Etc/UTC').
.SS Boot Loader Options
.TP
\f[B]\-ib\f[R], \f[B]\-\-initramfs\-builder\f[R] \f[I]NAME\f[R]
Specify the initramfs builder (`livekit' or `dracut').
.SS Boot Menu Options
.TP
\f[B]\-mln\f[R], \f[B]\-\-menu\-language\f[R] \f[I]NAME\f[R]
Specify the boot menu language (`multilang' for language selection or
specific language code like `ru_RU').
.SH DEFAULT SETTINGS
.SS Kernel Settings
\f[B]KERNEL_FLAVOUR\f[R]: \[lq]none\[rq]
.PP
\f[B]KERNEL_PROVIDER\f[R]: \[lq]distribution\[rq] (automatically
\[lq]minios\[rq] for Trixie/Excalibur i386)
.PP
\f[B]MINIOS_KERNEL_SERIES\f[R]: \[lq]auto\[rq]
.PP
\f[B]KERNEL_PAYLOAD_MODE\f[R]: \[lq]runtime\[rq]
.SS Locale & Timezone Settings
\f[B]LOCALE\f[R]: \[lq]en_US\[rq] \f[B]LIVE_TIMEZONE\f[R]:
\[lq]Etc/UTC\[rq]
.SS Boot Loader Settings
\f[B]INITRAMFS_BUILDER\f[R]: \[lq]dracut\[rq]
.SS Boot Menu Settings
\f[B]MENU_LANG\f[R]: \[lq]multilang\[rq]
.SH INTERACTION WITH MINIOS\-LIVE
\f[B]minios\-cmd\f[R] prepares the build environment and generates a
\f[B]build.conf\f[R] configuration file based on the options provided.
It then calls \f[B]minios\-live\f[R] with the relevant environment
variables, delegating the build execution to \f[B]minios\-live\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
Create a MiniOS Standard system image with default settings:
.IP
.EX
minios\-cmd \-d bookworm \-a amd64 \-de xfce \-pv standard \-c zstd \-mk \-dkms \-kl
.EE
.PP
Create a MiniOS Toolbox system image with default settings:
.IP
.EX
minios\-cmd \-d bookworm \-a amd64 \-de xfce \-pv toolbox \-c zstd \-mk \-dkms \-kl
.EE
.PP
Create a system image with Russian locale:
.IP
.EX
minios\-cmd \-d bookworm \-a amd64 \-de xfce \-pv toolbox \-l ru_RU
.EE
.PP
Create a system image with LXQt desktop environment:
.IP
.EX
minios\-cmd \-d bookworm \-a amd64 \-de lxqt \-pv standard
.EE
.PP
Create a system image for 32\-bit architecture:
.IP
.EX
minios\-cmd \-d buster \-a i386 \-de xfce \-pv standard
.EE
.PP
Create a system image with Ubuntu Jammy:
.IP
.EX
minios\-cmd \-d jammy \-pv standard \-a amd64 \-de xfce
.EE
.PP
Enable multilingual support (generates locales for English, Spanish,
German, French, Italian, Portuguese, Brazilian Portuguese, Russian, and
Indonesian):
.IP
.EX
minios\-cmd \-d trixie \-a amd64 \-de xfce \-pv standard \-ml
.EE
.PP
Create a system image with Russian boot menu language:
.IP
.EX
minios\-cmd \-d bookworm \-a amd64 \-de xfce \-pv standard \-mln ru_RU
.EE
.PP
Create a system image with livekit initramfs builder (smaller size):
.IP
.EX
minios\-cmd \-d bookworm \-a amd64 \-de flux \-pv standard \-ib livekit
.EE
.SH GENERATING AND USING CONFIGURATION FILES
Generate a configuration file:
.IP
.EX
minios\-cmd \-\-config\-only \-\-config\-file myconfig.conf \-d bookworm \-a amd64 \-de xfce \-pv standard
.EE
.PP
Use the configuration file with \f[B]minios\-live\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
BUILD_CONF=/path/to/myconfig.conf minios\-live \-
.EE
.PP
or:
.IP
.EX
export BUILD_CONF=/path/to/myconfig.conf
minios\-live \-
.EE
